IELTS.lesson({"test": 4, "part": 1, "title": "Test 4, Part 1 — the interview", "candidate": "rawan", "script": [{"who": "examiner", "text": "Good morning. Come in, have a seat.", "ar": "صباح الخير. تفضّلي بالدخول واجلسي.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/1b2def3fa2b0b362.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "My name is Mohamad Khorbatli. Can you tell me your full name, please?", "ar": "اسمي محمد خرباطلي. هل يمكنكِ أن تخبريني باسمكِ الكامل من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c756d0707f344069.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Rawan Saleh.", "ar": "روان صالح.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/202a3913fa1b9728.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "And what can I call you?", "ar": "وبماذا أناديكِ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/5085ae49113e09cf.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Rawan is fine.", "ar": "روان تكفي.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/7809f6ee14a67539.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you, Rawan. Can I see your identification, please?", "ar": "شكراً لكِ يا روان. هل يمكنني رؤية هويّتكِ من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/7986315afde9daa9.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Of course. Here you are.", "ar": "بالتأكيد. تفضّل.", "shot": null, "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/90c4791e3148c41e.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That's all fine.", "ar": "شكراً. كل شيء على ما يرام.", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a65ff8d3eccec277.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Now, in this first part I'd like to ask you some questions about yourself. Let's talk about technology.", "ar": "الآن، في هذا الجزء الأول أودّ أن أطرح عليكِ بعض الأسئلة عنكِ. لنتحدّث عن التكنولوجيا.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/b456427512d8d541.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you use a computer every day?", "ar": "هل تستخدمين الحاسوب كلّ يوم؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/6808cc38923ab4a2.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Every day, all day. It's my actual job, I'm a designer. So if the laptop dies I don't have a profession, and with the power in Damascus that's a slightly alarming thing to notice out loud.", "ar": "كلّ يوم، طوال اليوم. هذا عملي فعلاً، أنا مصمّمة. فإذا تعطّل الحاسوب المحمول لا تبقى لي مهنة، ومع وضع الكهرباء في دمشق فإنّ قول ذلك بصوت عالٍ أمر مقلق قليلاً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/c865bed1eb6d6ffa.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "What's the most useful piece of technology you own?", "ar": "ما أكثر جهاز تقني تملكينه فائدةً؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/765a57089b0d6891.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "The laptop, obviously, but actually I'd say the power bank. People think that's a joke and it isn't. When the electricity goes in the middle of a call with a client in Germany, the thing that saves the job isn't the computer.", "ar": "الحاسوب المحمول طبعاً، لكنّي في الحقيقة أقول بطّاريّة الشحن المتنقّلة. يظنّ الناس أنّ هذه مزحة وهي ليست كذلك. حين تنقطع الكهرباء في منتصف مكالمة مع زبون في ألمانيا، فإنّ ما ينقذ العمل ليس الحاسوب.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/9f15125a54594154.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Has technology changed the way you work?", "ar": "هل غيّرت التكنولوجيا طريقة عملكِ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/5d376262efae42dc.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "It is the way I work. The thing is, I've never had a job that wasn't like this. I've never been in an office and I've never met most of the people who pay me, so I can't really compare. I've worked this way since university. This is just what work is.", "ar": "هي طريقة عملي. المسألة أنّني لم يكن لي يوماً عمل غير هذا. لم أعمل في مكتب قطّ ولم ألتقِ معظم من يدفعون لي، فلا أستطيع أن أقارن فعلاً. أعمل بهذه الطريقة منذ الجامعة. هذا هو العمل بالنسبة لي.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/7132d905ba14d7b9.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Are there any disadvantages to it?", "ar": "هل لذلك أيّ مساوئ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/ab7491119ea85b2f.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Oh, loads. The obvious one is that you never stop, because there's no building you leave. But the one nobody talks about, I think, is that you're completely alone with your own judgement. Nobody in my building is going to walk past your screen and say that's not working.", "ar": "كثيرة جداً. الواضح منها أنّكِ لا تتوقّفين أبداً، لأنّه لا يوجد مبنى تغادرينه. لكنّ ما لا يتحدّث عنه أحد، في رأيي، أنّكِ وحيدة تماماً مع حكمكِ الخاص. لا أحد في مبنانا سيمرّ بجانب شاشتكِ ويقول إنّ هذا لا ينجح.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/38b3385ebd70c6c0.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Let's move on to talk about mobile phones.", "ar": "لننتقل للحديث عن الهواتف المحمولة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/9aa2c64e2de3d556.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "How often do you use your phone?", "ar": "كم مرّة تستخدمين هاتفكِ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/43894ac08d2a57bf.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Constantly, and I've stopped pretending otherwise. I did one of those weeks where you check the screen time and then feel terrible about it, and honestly nothing changed except that now I know the number. It's worse on the days the power's out, which is most of them.", "ar": "باستمرار، وقد كففت عن التظاهر بغير ذلك. جرّبت واحداً من تلك الأسابيع التي تتفقّدين فيها وقت الشاشة ثمّ تشعرين بالسوء حياله، وبصراحة لم يتغيّر شيء سوى أنّني صرت أعرف الرقم. والأمر أسوأ في الأيّام التي تنقطع فيها الكهرباء، وهي معظمها.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/35efa8f2aae05954.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "What do you use it for most?", "ar": "فيمَ تستخدمينه أكثر شيء؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/027b1d3c36cebf59.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Work, annoyingly. If it were all friends and photos I'd feel better about it. It's clients, invoices and chasing payment, so the office comes with me everywhere, including Friday lunch at my mother's.", "ar": "للعمل، وهذا مزعج. لو كان كلّه أصدقاء وصوراً لشعرت بشعور أفضل حياله. إنّه زبائن وفواتير وملاحقة للدفعات، فالمكتب يأتي معي إلى كلّ مكان، بما في ذلك غداء الجمعة عند أمي.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/d71d7bd3455e225c.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Could you manage without a phone for a week?", "ar": "هل يمكنكِ أن تدبّري أمركِ بلا هاتف لمدّة أسبوع؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/4d8cddba1cd0859b.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Manage, yes. Afford to, no. A week with no phone means a week of not answering clients, and the thing about freelancing in Damascus is that silence costs you the next job, not just this one. So I've never tried it and I don't plan to.", "ar": "أدبّر أمري، نعم. أتحمّل كلفة ذلك، لا. أسبوع بلا هاتف يعني أسبوعاً دون الردّ على الزبائن، والمسألة في العمل الحرّ في دمشق أنّ الصمت يكلّفكِ العمل القادم، لا هذا العمل وحده. لذلك لم أجرّب ذلك قطّ ولا أنوي أن أجرّبه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/a2c998f7d8bc383e.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you think children should have phones?", "ar": "هل تظنّين أنّه ينبغي أن يكون للأطفال هواتف؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/ee68e07bd62f6606.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "I don't know, honestly, and I don't trust anybody who's certain about it. My sister's twelve and has one, and the arguments against are all completely true, and so is the fact that my mother can find her.", "ar": "لا أعرف بصراحة، ولا أثق بأحد واثق من جوابه في هذا. أختي عمرها اثنتا عشرة سنة ولديها هاتف، والحجج المعارضة صحيحة تماماً كلّها، وكذلك حقيقة أنّ أمي تستطيع أن تجدها.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/7ba58e203883228f.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Finally in this part, let's talk about neighbours.", "ar": "وأخيراً في هذا الجزء، لنتحدّث عن الجيران.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/b2e2bc49f63fb0b7.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you know your neighbours well?", "ar": "هل تعرفين جيرانكِ جيّداً؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/98cc2703ef993f37.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Honestly, better than I'd choose to. It's one stairwell and five flats in our building, so everyone knows when anyone's internet is down, because we all complain at the same time on the stairs.", "ar": "بصراحة، أكثر مما أختار. إنّه درج واحد وخمس شقق في مبنانا، فيعرف الجميع حين ينقطع الإنترنت عن أيّ أحد، لأنّنا جميعاً نشكو في الوقت نفسه على الدرج.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/de11d89fc4d14a4a.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you think it's important to have good neighbours?", "ar": "هل تظنّين أنّ وجود جيران طيّبين أمر مهمّ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/1574a657126a4e8c.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "More important here than people from somewhere else would assume, I think. The thing is, a lot of what makes a building work isn't official. Who pays the generator man, who has the key to the roof. That only works if people are speaking, and here they're speaking all the time.", "ar": "أهمّ هنا مما قد يفترضه من هم من مكان آخر، في رأيي. المسألة أنّ كثيراً مما يجعل المبنى يعمل ليس رسمياً. من يدفع لصاحب المولّدة، ومن عنده مفتاح السطح. وهذا لا ينجح إلّا إذا كان الناس يتكلّمون، وهنا هم يتكلّمون طوال الوقت.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/5073f8a52face058.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "How have neighbourhoods changed since you were a child?", "ar": "كيف تغيّرت الأحياء منذ كنتِ طفلة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/1b97afa2e6f1b726.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "People move more, so you don't get the twenty-year neighbour any more. Actually that cuts both ways. My mother could tell you the history of every family on her street, and some of those families would rather she couldn't.", "ar": "الناس ينتقلون أكثر، فلم يعد هناك الجار الذي يبقى عشرين سنة. في الحقيقة لهذا وجهان. أمي تستطيع أن تحدّثك عن تاريخ كلّ عائلة في شارعها، وبعض تلك العائلات كانت تفضّل لو أنّها لا تستطيع.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/c816a056684ea941.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Would you prefer to live somewhere quieter?", "ar": "هل تفضّلين العيش في مكان أهدأ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/7b4d8d1ab7ffd7ed.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "I say yes about once a week and honestly I'd last a fortnight. I've tried working somewhere silent, at my aunt's place outside the city, and I got nothing done, which was humiliating and quite useful to find out.", "ar": "أقول نعم مرّة في الأسبوع تقريباً، وبصراحة كنت سأصمد أسبوعين. جرّبت العمل في مكان صامت، في بيت خالتي خارج المدينة، ولم أنجز شيئاً، وكان ذلك مذلّاً ومفيداً جداً أن أكتشفه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/c603f18d5cb59dda.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That is the end of Part One.", "ar": "شكراً لكِ. بهذا ينتهي القسم الأول.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/50f379466faf1658.mp3"}], "boxes": [{"q": "Do you use a computer every day?", "ar": null, "topic": "Technology", "model": "Every day, all day. It's my actual job, I'm a designer. So if the laptop dies I don't have a profession, and with the power in Damascus that's a slightly alarming thing to notice out loud.", "why": "Answers in four words and then says why it matters. The last clause is self-aware without being a performance."}, {"q": "What's the most useful piece of technology you own?", "ar": null, "topic": "Technology", "model": "The laptop, obviously, but actually I'd say the power bank. People think that's a joke and it isn't. When the electricity goes in the middle of a call with a client in Germany, the thing that saves the job isn't the computer.", "why": "Picks the unexpected object and then earns it with one concrete scene. Germany and the power cut do the whole job."}, {"q": "Has technology changed the way you work?", "ar": null, "topic": "Technology", "model": "It is the way I work. The thing is, I've never had a job that wasn't like this. I've never been in an office and I've never met most of the people who pay me, so I can't really compare. I've worked this way since university. This is just what work is.", "why": "Refuses the comparison the question assumes, and says why she can't make it. That is a band 7 move: answer the question you can actually answer."}, {"q": "Are there any disadvantages to it?", "ar": null, "topic": "Technology", "model": "Oh, loads. The obvious one is that you never stop, because there's no building you leave. But the one nobody talks about, I think, is that you're completely alone with your own judgement. Nobody in my building is going to walk past your screen and say that's not working.", "why": "Gives the obvious disadvantage, names it as obvious, then supplies the one she has actually felt. The ordering is the skill."}, {"q": "How often do you use your phone?", "ar": null, "topic": "Mobile phones", "model": "Constantly, and I've stopped pretending otherwise. I did one of those weeks where you check the screen time and then feel terrible about it, and honestly nothing changed except that now I know the number. It's worse on the days the power's out, which is most of them.", "why": "A confession with a number behind it, and the power cut keeps it in her life rather than anybody's."}, {"q": "What do you use it for most?", "ar": null, "topic": "Mobile phones", "model": "Work, annoyingly. If it were all friends and photos I'd feel better about it. It's clients, invoices and chasing payment, so the office comes with me everywhere, including Friday lunch at my mother's.", "why": "Three nouns and a consequence. The list is what makes it hers and not a general complaint about phones."}, {"q": "Could you manage without a phone for a week?", "ar": null, "topic": "Mobile phones", "model": "Manage, yes. Afford to, no. A week with no phone means a week of not answering clients, and the thing about freelancing in Damascus is that silence costs you the next job, not just this one. So I've never tried it and I don't plan to.", "why": "Two words, then the reason. 'Silence costs you the next job' is the whole economics of freelancing in one clause."}, {"q": "Do you think children should have phones?", "ar": null, "topic": "Mobile phones", "model": "I don't know, honestly, and I don't trust anybody who's certain about it. My sister's twelve and has one, and the arguments against are all completely true, and so is the fact that my mother can find her.", "why": "Holds two true things at once without resolving them, which is what the question deserves."}, {"q": "Do you know your neighbours well?", "ar": null, "topic": "Neighbours", "model": "Honestly, better than I'd choose to. It's one stairwell and five flats in our building, so everyone knows when anyone's internet is down, because we all complain at the same time on the stairs.", "why": "A specific building, a specific number of flats, and a shared complaint. Nothing here could be about anywhere else."}, {"q": "Do you think it's important to have good neighbours?", "ar": null, "topic": "Neighbours", "model": "More important here than people from somewhere else would assume, I think. The thing is, a lot of what makes a building work isn't official. Who pays the generator man, who has the key to the roof. That only works if people are speaking, and here they're speaking all the time.", "why": "Moves from an opinion to the mechanism underneath it. The generator man and the roof key are evidence, not decoration."}, {"q": "How have neighbourhoods changed since you were a child?", "ar": null, "topic": "Neighbours", "model": "People move more, so you don't get the twenty-year neighbour any more. Actually that cuts both ways. My mother could tell you the history of every family on her street, and some of those families would rather she couldn't.", "why": "Concedes the change, then turns it with 'that cuts both ways'. The last clause is funny and slightly sharp."}, {"q": "Would you prefer to live somewhere quieter?", "ar": null, "topic": "Neighbours", "model": "I say yes about once a week and honestly I'd last a fortnight. I've tried working somewhere silent, at my aunt's place outside the city, and I got nothing done, which was humiliating and quite useful to find out.", "why": "Tests her own claim against something she actually did, and reports the result against herself."}], "voices": {"examiner": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "candidate": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120"}});
